        "**Red retrotympanic mass**: glomus tympanicum (blanches with pneumatic pressure, Brown sign), aberrant ICA (anteroinferior, never biopsy), persistent stapedial artery or a high dehiscent jugular bulb (blue, posteroinferior) (Cummings 7e, Ch 153)",
        "**DAVF**: objective bruit over the mastoid or occiput, sometimes after trauma, pregnancy or sinus thrombosis. Headache, new neurologic deficit or cognitive decline suggests cortical venous drainage (Cummings 7e, Ch 136)",
        "**Direct CCF**: days to weeks after head trauma, pulsatile proptosis, chemosis, conjunctival injection, orbital bruit, ophthalmoplegia (often CN VI) and falling vision (Cummings 7e, Ch 136)",
